WEBVTT
NOTE OpenIE Research TV — spellcheck (30s) Narrator Matilda

1
00:00:00.260 --> 00:00:01.265
Forty years ago,

2
00:00:01.265 --> 00:00:07.423
checking spelling on a personal computer required buying a separate hundred-dollar floppy package.

3
00:00:07.843 --> 00:00:10.837
Spell check became free not through charity,

4
00:00:10.837 --> 00:00:15.668
but because compressed dictionaries dropped per-word compute near zero.

5
00:00:16.088 --> 00:00:19.056
A skill used on every sentence belongs inside

6
00:00:19.056 --> 00:00:23.277
the operating system—provided running it costs negligible watts.

7
00:00:23.697 --> 00:00:30.884
Computer intelligence reaches seven billion people when common skills compile down to spell-check-scale energy.
